{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_136be139d93078e7a01a6a3da4340afd8ac1775984948462c464518f733e0261","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b94c7bc2e096c708fbbb61432656325f39740b8e2151ef905b67f2324bc097c1"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"The benchmark comprises 113 tasks spanning TypeScript, Go, Python, JavaScript, and Rust, with isolated environments and program-based verifiers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2fbca97b9da7abbbdbfff1842c20f3361eaf18397db44760d59072a7e2291891","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0bdc1f5cea0fe6a38f2e04da3d5ae6dc209147653ad1c8eed034a6109f960d5c"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"The verifier accepts any solution whose observable behavior is correct, regardless of internal symbol names or structure, and the reference patch is never used at grading time.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3bab233abd5bfce5d559362fcd663fcc102bdc351189e2f0c54bac19294f78b4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2803db14a2f0e9284e9cc355d8bf4056833fc8935887d61c23b351a4276053e6"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Pier, a Harbor-compatible eval framework, adds per-agent network allowlists so agents get only needed network access while the task environment stays isolated, unlike Harbor's blanket blocking in no-internet tasks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4e2ddcdbd7f515d20e8eda03065f1b7aaa7f47bf30f95f4f8afe97870be2bcfa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e563bfc552529c2dd0e4e17b2dac941afbdb0bf3eb7ff39644d71f0da263ba3e"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Since v1.1, grading uses Harbor's separate verifier environment: the agent works in isolation, commits its work, and a collect hook extracts commits as a patch applied and graded in a pristine container.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4f8d0980b671bc30ae0fa074f068644e8b893ca12730f6368ec6bb70c3cba0b9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b94c7bc2e096c708fbbb61432656325f39740b8e2151ef905b67f2324bc097c1"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"DeepSWE is a benchmark measuring frontier coding agents on original, long-horizon software engineering tasks drawn from active open-source repositories.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_515b61b28c01e6812634967f1ccbeb0fd8d71c2f79a74584035395d6e6d7dc91","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b4d9f8d119580dc8705d31a6f5dbdd6ea374692832fe3574d91ba5fd4bb0a5a","slc_154ec38fed256346c30f61729d2642c7bfd8f35cd2eba8d8a69a27f13bf5892b"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Tasks use the Harbor task format, with task.toml metadata, instruction.md, an environment Dockerfile, tests, and a held-out reference solution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_58ecac9b533fb9cb23ab9c69e876737673c814a7041cc6c063b58809fd54316e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8147dc3a20d7ab56a343546c8973279f3820a9c70557f27eec007e8ea5c149a2"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Each run produces verifier outputs including reward.json with binary reward and pass fractions, ctrf.json test reports, raw stdout logs, and framework-native grader reports.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_75b0561525b3a82ece80d1a6854b68c9d92d9bb998173737e7193788fc3d7f8d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0009b714563f11e8df80778a667154903eea7c395ecc59e18f8c57555b8c7fd7","slc_039810005020ddd8e8b40d24f0f34b162674b7d21cc0483220dd5e6a970e0b48","slc_3e4b35bd308eb0bbb9f22a6e300f8bbe1706434d170ea7b1ed1c6b114a21d16f","slc_fee5c1921834b0aea5dc68a85a3814ebede125b192f544628a91070704aabe46"],"source_ids":["src_196eb803adf45eca8275646a354c3c31"],"text":"Tasks derive from upstream open-source projects under permissive licenses (e.g., MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause); the repo's Apache-2.0 license covers only Datacurve's original contributions, not upstream code.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ecfb844fd722440ca026adccddf7966888d4332354a78d8cee5935bb344eac3b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_496cc50f8542cf9c6fd81210f0e8d5a3263ef353a1dca1ef669db8b905533b3a","slc_caa24315c4ab930c54a40a85d167334a28fc8e7805d3710d8a4450c36b9a3873","slc_da9b072391756db1b601f570b0641375624652676cad4a7317fa35bd8a761b0f","slc_df2a7c705728ec1b30f55d5d2fa2c693203e016eeb9dba5f1667a6b0fb571c40"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"The benchmark is run via Pier, installed with uv, using commands like 'pier run -p deep-swe/tasks --agent mini-swe-agent' with model-specific API keys exported.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f21fc26059000f3bae36d300a3ca2a4c9f2d891a937f157c9ad11552d6d78c26","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_400411b3af763a66d96df12362961191ddbb86cdec6f079b8f16f078105ebc68","slc_58b23a22a0941200aefb028f5b07d758d2f8c52bb4d6efb28667984984865989","slc_ca31cfa863534423fdc392841d41a556427d923a76ebdc4a0385cf75beb6f3eb"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Runs can be subsetted deterministically via --n-tasks with --sample-seed, or targeted at a single task by passing a task-id path to pier run.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f4bd4e999040000f03c5c6adad572761915de4b5be2b26ab519f93c7aab8a303","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e563bfc552529c2dd0e4e17b2dac941afbdb0bf3eb7ff39644d71f0da263ba3e"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"The separate-verifier grading flow requires the datacurve-pier package at a version newer than 0.3.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ffede67f18689a3bb68db8c95fed03885addb7a11120a43100c4a8e6e3139ae8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe@0b9fabbb63b9 snapshot a2fc1feb8fd2295f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_19276c95340d044dbe71db319c8e7676d9691d91d1f40ade39a5468d04b5cecd"],"source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"text":"Pier supports multiple agents: mini-swe-agent is model-agnostic, and Pier also drives claude-code, codex, gemini-cli, and opencode; --env modal runs parallel sandboxes on Modal.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
